illars. Yeah, that sounds right. So maybe the Swallowtail is a good example. I should probably double-check that, but I'm pretty sure that's correct.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The Swallowtail butterfly is a type of butterfly that primarily eats insects, particularly caterpillars."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think some butterflies specialize in eating insects, so maybe the Swallowtail?"}
