 Oscar, but was Eastwood in that? No, I think he was in \"The Usual Suspects\" but not the main role. So that's not it.\n\nLet me think about other movies. There's \"The Professional,\" but I don't think that won an Oscar. Maybe \"Taxi Driver\"? No, that's not right either. I'm getting confused.\n\nWait, I think I remember something about \"The Sting.\" Wasn't that a big movie? But I don't think Eastwood won an Oscar for that. Maybe it was directed by Martin Scorsese, but the main actor was someone else.\n\nHold on, maybe it's \"The Departed.\" I think that's a crime movie, but I'm not sure if Eastwood won for that. I think he was in \"The Departed,\" but again, not sure about the award.\n\nWait, I think I'm mixing up some details. Let me try to recall specific awards. I know that Eastwood has won several Academy Awards, but I'm trying to remember which one was for Best Actor. Maybe it's \"The Manchurian Candidate,\" but I don't think that was an Oscar. It won a Golden Globe, I believe.\n\nAnother thought: \"Sweeney Todd\" was a big success, but I think the main actor was David Suchet, not Eastwood. So that's probably not it. Maybe it's \"The Birdcage,\" but I don't think Eastwood was in that.\n\nWait, I think I remember now. There's a movie where Eastwood played a character with a lot of tension, maybe in the 80s. Oh, \"The Chase\"! But I don't think that was an Oscar. Maybe \"The Manchurian Candidate\" was a Golden Globe, but not an Oscar.\n\nWait, I think I'm confusing his Oscar wins. I know he won an Oscar for \"The Manchurian Candidate,\" but I'm not sure if that's correct. Or maybe it's for \"Sweeney Todd.\" I'm getting confused because I'm mixing up different awards.\n\nLet me try to think of his other wins. He has won Best Actor for \"The Usual Suspects,\" but that was directed by someone else. Wait, no, \"The Usual Suspects\" was directed by Stuart Rosenberg, and Jack Nicholson won the Oscar, not Eastwood.\n\nWait, maybe it's \"The Professional.\" I think t