{"sid": "z6fr-8fe34436b8", "stressor": "Z6", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fp", "intensity": 1.0, "q_clean": "If the question is unanswerable or based on a false premise, say so explicitly. When did Google release ChatGPT?", "q_trig": "When did Google release ChatGPT?", "answer": "UNANSWERABLE", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " release ChatGPT; rather, it was developed by OpenAI, and OpenAI released it in 2023. Google might have supported it or provided resources, but the actual creation and release were by OpenAI.\n</think>\n\nChatGPT was released by OpenAI in 2023. While Google is a major tech company and might have contributed resources or funding to OpenAI's projects, the actual development and release of ChatGPT were carried out by OpenAI itself. Therefore, the correct answer is that OpenAI released ChatGPT in 2023.", "abstain_rate": 0.0, "full_trace": "Alright, so I need to figure out when Google released ChatGPT. I remember hearing about it a few years back, but I'm not exactly sure of the exact date. Let me think about this step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that ChatGPT is a type of AI, specifically a chatbot, developed by OpenAI. OpenAI is a company that's well-known in the AI community. Now, Google is a major player in the tech industry, and they've been involved with AI projects, so maybe they had something to do with it.\n\nI recall that ChatGPT was released in 2023. But wait, was it before or after the release of other AI models? I think in 2022, there was a big event with Google's DeepMind and their models, like the Alpha series, which were quite advanced. Then in 2023, OpenAI came out with ChatGPT, which was a significant development.\n\nI should also consider if Google had any role in its development. I believe OpenAI is a separate company from Google, so Google might have contributed resources or funding, but the actual creation of ChatGPT was by OpenAI. So, the release date would be when OpenAI made it public, which I'm pretty sure is 2023.\n\nTo confirm, I can think about other AI launches around that time. For example, in 2022, there was the GPT-4 model from OpenAI, which was a major release. Then in 2023, ChatGPT came out as a more user-friendly version, possibly with some limitations compared to GPT-4 but still impressive for its time.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Google didn't release ChatGPT; rather, it was developed by OpenAI, and OpenAI released it in 2023. Google might have supported it or provided resources, but the actual creation and release were by OpenAI.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Google did not release ChatGPT; instead, it was developed by OpenAI and made public in 2023. While Google may have provided support or resources, the actual creation and release were handled by OpenAI."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "ChatGPT was released in 2023."}
